{
  "manufacturer": "Janitza",
  "manufacturer_slug": "janitza",
  "model": "UMG 511 power quality analyser (Modbus RTU)",
  "model_slug": "umg-511",
  "short_model": "UMG 511",
  "aliases": [
    "UMG511",
    "UMG 511",
    "Janitza UMG511"
  ],
  "equipment_type": "Power meter (power quality analyser)",
  "applies_to": "UMG 511 per Modbus address list 1.037.021.9.g (05/2021).",
  "summary": "The UMG 511 is Janitza's power quality analyser. As a Modbus slave it serves its whole address list as big-endian values that include the CT/VT ratios. This map covers the 19000-19120 'frequently required readings' block (voltages, currents, powers, CosPhi, frequency, energies, THD), system time, internal temperature and the energy-reset commands.",
  "transport": [
    "RTU"
  ],
  "defaults": {
    "unit_id": null,
    "baud": null,
    "parity": "None",
    "data_bits": 8,
    "stop_bits": 2,
    "tcp_port": null
  },
  "addressing": {
    "convention": "0-based",
    "note": "Addresses are printed as the protocol address and sent unchanged: 19000 is requested as 19000. The date/time list starts at address 0 (_REALTIME), which only fits 0-based numbering. In a 1-based or Modicon tool enter 19001 / 419001."
  },
  "default_word_order": "ABCD",
  "firmware": null,
  "source": {
    "title": "Power Quality Analyser UMG 511 - Modbus-address and Formulary",
    "doc_number": "1.037.021.9.g",
    "revision_date": "2021-05",
    "url": "https://shop.fortop.co.uk/files/umg511fortopjanitzamodbusaddressliste1295013212757.pdf",
    "unofficial": true,
    "pages": "Functions and transfer parameters pp. 4-5; frequently required readings p. 12; date and time p. 13; internal temperature p. 17; other values p. 44"
  },
  "notes": [
    "Janitza does not appear to host this address list at a public URL; this is an unaltered copy of the Janitza document (doc. no. 1.037.021.9.g) on a UK distributor's site.",
    "Byte order: the listed addresses return big-endian data (high word first = ABCD); adding 32768 to an address returns the same value little-endian.",
    "Transfer parameters (p. 5): 9.6-921.6 kbps, 8 data bits, no parity; the UMG 511 sends 2 stop bits. No default baud rate or device address is given.",
    "19068 in the frequently-read block is the tariff 1 (rate 1) consumed total only, so it is left out.",
    "Left out: the per-channel energy arrays from 6546 (only element [0] is labelled, so the meaning of the other elements is not stated), the 64-bit _REALTIME at 0, min/max/mean blocks, harmonics and configuration registers.",
    "The digital-output and delete rows have no RD/WR column in the 'Other values' table; access is taken from their descriptions."
  ],
